      "id": "ideas",
      "type": "explain",
      "title": "How linked lists work",
      "points": [
        "Each **node** stores a value and a reference, `next`, to the following node. The last node’s `next` is `null`.",
        "`head` points to the first node. Lose it and you lose the whole list.",
        "Walking: `for (Node cur = head; cur != null; cur = cur.next)`. Reaching item i takes **O(i)**, with no `a[i]`.",
        "Inserting at the front is **O(1)**: point the new node at the old head, then move head."
      ],
      "pattern": "Node n = new Node(x);\nn.next = head;  // link to the old first node\nhead = n;       // n is the new first node"
    },
